  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A disc of mass M and radius R is on a horizontal frictionless table. Two equal and opposite forces, each of magnitude F, act on the disc. The moment of inertia of the disc about its axis is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{2}MR^{2}\"></span>.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>What is the angular acceleration of the disc?</p>\n<p>[1]</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\">0</li><li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{F}{MR}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{2F}{MR}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{4F}{MR}\"></span></li></ol>"
  },
